  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a severe upward bias when recent history shows high volatility or a downward trend followed by a spike; forecasts consistently overshoot true outcomes by 5-10% in the first 10 days.",
    "When sentiment history contains isolated positive spikes (e.g., 0.20-0.40) amidst neutral periods, the model fails to capture immediate mean reversion and instead projects a linear upward drift that contradicts actual price consolidation.",
    "Forecasts systematically underestimate the magnitude of subsequent rallies; true outcomes often reach 15-20% higher than predicted within 30 days when recent history ends near local lows.",
    "The model ignores short-term momentum reversals, projecting smooth growth even when sentiment signals mixed or declining, leading to significant negative errors during the first half of the forecast horizon.",
    "Apply a downward correction factor of approximately -8% to the initial forecast value if the last 3 days of history show a decline and sentiment is neutral or slightly positive."
  ]
}
